     - None of these conclusions contradict the rabbit\u2019s inability to see the lion.\n\n3. **Contradiction Prevention**:  \n   - If the rabbit saw the lion, it would violate statement 19 (since it is not big). Thus, the rabbit **must not see the lion**.\n\n**Conclusion**: The statement \"The rabbit does not see the lion\" is **true**. Therefore, the correct option is:\n\n**Answer**: A) True",
